<title>UK: TI Group year underlying profits rise 16 pct.</title>
<headline>TI Group year underlying profits rise 16 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Dec 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		34.1		   vs 26.5</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 9.75		   vs 8.75</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 14.5		   vs 13.1</p>
<p> Pretax		     232.2		  vs 184.8</p>
<p> Pre-exceptional profit 211.1		  vs 181.6</p>
<p> Exceptionals	     21.1 GAIN	    vs 3.2 GAIN</p>
<p> Turnover		   1,757		  vs 1,703</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits for the engineering group to range between 208 and 215 million stg before exceptional gains from disposals. Dividend forecasts predicted a final dividend of around 9.55 pence, making 14.3 pence for the year, up from 13.1 pence in 1995.</p>
<p>Full company name - TI Group Plc</p>
</text>
